    <detaileddescription>
<para>A crash-consistent, byte-addressable memory pool backed by PMem.</para>
<para>Layout within the mapped region: [ PMemPoolHeader (256 B) | AllocBitmap | Data arena ]</para>
<para>The header and bitmap are persisted with clwb+sfence after every allocation so the pool can be recovered after a crash.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: all public methods are thread-safe via an internal CAS-based bump allocator. Concurrent frees are supported via the bitmap. The pool does NOT support arbitrary in-place reuse of freed blocks (append-only with compaction via rebuild()). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
